<div class="row mb-2">
    <div class="col-12">
        <div class="card border-primary shadow-sm">
            <div class="card-header bg-light text-primary fw-bold d-flex justify-content-between align-items-center">
                <span>
                    <i class="mdi mdi-information-outline me-2"></i> Overdraft Activation Request Steps
                </span>
                <button class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-primary" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#overdraftGuidelinesBody">
                    <i class="mdi mdi-chevron-down"></i>
                </button>
            </div>

            <div id="overdraftGuidelinesBody" class="collapse show">
                <div class="card-body">
                    <ul class="mb-3 list-unstyled">

                        <!-- 🔍 Filter/Search -->
                        <li class="mb-2">
                            <i class="mdi mdi-filter-outline text-secondary me-2"></i>
                            <strong>1. Filter Requests:</strong> Use the top filter panel to locate requests by <code>Status</code>, <code>Branch</code>, <code>Customer ID</code>, or date range.
                        </li>

                        <!-- 👁️ View -->
                        <li class="mb-2">
                            <i class="mdi mdi-eye-outline text-info me-2"></i>
                            <strong>2. View Request:</strong> Click the <i class="mdi mdi-eye-outline text-info"></i> icon to see full request details including account, limit, interest rate, and recovery method.
                        </li>

                        <!-- ✅ Approve -->
                        <li class="mb-2">
                            <i class="mdi mdi-check-bold text-success me-2"></i>
                            <strong>3. Approve Request:</strong> Approving confirms the request meets all internal criteria and makes the overdraft facility eligible for activation.
                        </li>

                        <!-- ❌ Reject -->
                        <li class="mb-2">
                            <i class="mdi mdi-close-thick text-danger me-2"></i>
                            <strong>4. Reject Request:</strong> Use the <i class="mdi mdi-close-thick text-danger"></i> icon to deny any non-compliant or invalid request.
                        </li>

                        <!-- 🚀 Activate -->
                        <li class="mb-2">
                            <i class="mdi mdi-check-decagram text-primary me-2"></i>
                            <strong>5. Activate Facility:</strong> Some requests may require a final manual activation after approval, depending on the overdraft configuration rules.
                        </li>

                        <!-- 📥 New Request -->
                        <li class="mb-2">
                            <i class="mdi mdi-plus-circle-outline text-muted me-2"></i>
                            <strong>6. Submit New:</strong> Use the <code>New Request</code> button to start a new activation linked to a valid customer and account.
                        </li>
                    </ul>

                    <div class="alert alert-warning d-flex align-items-center" role="alert">
                        <i class="mdi mdi-alert-circle-outline me-2 fs-4 text-warning"></i>
                        <div>
                            <strong>Important:</strong> If an overdraft request is not validated and approved, the overdraft service will remain unavailable for the customer. Always ensure requests go through proper review and approval before expecting activation.
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <p class="text-muted mb-0">
                        <i class="mdi mdi-shield-check-outline me-2"></i>
                        Align all approvals with credit policy, product rules, and authorization limits defined by your branch or institution.
                    </p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
